o}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-kus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-kus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-kus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-kus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-kus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-25T17:24:12Z","updated_at":"2025-10-25T17:24:12Z","body":"Thank you for the thoughtful feedback and for explaining the design philosophy around error messages. I appreciate your perspective about keeping them concise and avoiding enumeration of all possible solutions.\n\nI completely understand that there are many ways to handle NaN values, and pandas shouldn't attempt to list them all. My main concern was that beginners often don't know about the existence of nullable integer types (Int64), which is the most pandas-idiomatic solution for this specific error.\n\nIf you'd be open to a more minimal approach, perhaps just mentioning nullable integers could help users discover this feature:","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/comments/3446917350/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ADITYA-kus","id":196836206,"node_id":"U_kgDOC7t7bg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196836206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-kus","html_url":"https://github.com/ADITYA-kus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-kus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-kus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-kus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-kus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://a